        "cooked": "<p>Omfg, the Pecos Bill stuff, I’m dying… <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/joy.png?v=12\" title=\":joy:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":joy:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Having listened for about fifteen or sixteen months forward from this point, when those episodes came out, I don’t know whether or not we ever got the stuff they cut from this conversation, before the AB Stormalong and Robert Johnson parts.</p>\n<p>I wonder who the Whaley and Goff equivalents of our modern age might be.  I don’t think we should say anything about it, it’s not a discussion we should have, I just invite the thought to live in your head, and answer the question for yourself to yourself.</p>\n<p>I mean, foxes can be silver, and gorillas can be silverbacks…</p>\n<p>I didn’t know Jack and the Beanstalk was an 18th century story; I always assumed it was from the same era as Robin Hood and Reynard the Fox.</p>\n<p>I now want a sexier version of Perestroika’s Iron Curtain who calls herself Soft Concrete.</p>",
